  {% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>{% endif %}
<h3>Each village</h3>
{% endif %}
{% if b.villages and b.villages.villages and b.worldpop %}
<p class="note">Villages whose area includes mapped flood, largest flood area first. People are from WorldPop 2020 (a modelled estimate, not a count): "in the village" covers the part of the village inside the corridor; "in the flood" is the people WorldPop puts on the village's flooded cells. Risk is relative and for this corridor only (flood, people in it and the village's vulnerability class); it is not a probability of loss. "Share in flood" is the mapped flood as a share of the whole village area. Inside or touching the mapped flood does not mean damaged. The 2011 Census figures are in {{ b.villages_csv }}.</p>
