<h2>Roads</h2>
{% if b.roads %}
<div class="about"><b>What this shows.</b> The length of OpenStreetMap roads whose centre line runs through mapped flood cells, by road class, and the named roads with the most length in the flood.</div>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Road class (OpenStreetMap)</th><th class="r">Length in the mapped flood (km)</th><th class="r">Length in the corridor (km)</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for r in b.road_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.cls }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.flood }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.total }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
{% if b.roads.top_named %}<h3>Named roads with the most length in the flood</h3>
<table><thead><tr><th>Road</th><th>Class</th><th class="r">Length in the flood (km)</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for r in b.roads.top_named[:10] %}<tr><td>{{ r.name }}</td><td>{{ r.class }}</td><td class="r">{{ "%.3f"|format(r.flood_km) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>{% endif %}
<p class="note">Roads &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). A road counts as in the flood where its centre line crosses a flood cell; bridges and raised roads may be counted although they stayed dry.</p>
{% else %}<p>Roads not available (run <code>python jalsar.py roads</code> once with the internet on).</p>{% endif %}

<h2 class="pb">How far the map has been checked</h2>
<div class="about"><b>How the checking works.</b> For two floods (October 2021 and August 2023) the flood was drawn by hand from Sentinel-2 optical images in eight windows along the corridor. Each model's map is compared with these drawings cell by cell. <b>Precision</b> is the share of the mapped flood that is real; <b>recall</b> is the share of the real flood that was mapped; <b>F1</b> joins the two into one number from 0 (no match) to 1 (perfect match). The 95 % interval comes from redrawing the eight windows at random 2,000 times, so it shows how much the score depends on which windows happened to be drawn.</div>
{% if b.validation %}
<p>The {{ b.validation.year }} event has hand-drawn reference maps in {{ b.n_windows }} windows along the corridor. Each model's map was scored against them with the project's scorer. F1 combines how much of the real flood was found (recall) and how much of the mapped flood was real (precision); the brackets give the 95 % interval from resampling the windows.</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Table</th><th>Reach</th><th class="r">F1 (95 % interval)</th><th class="r">Precision</th><th class="r">Recall</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for r in b.val_rows %}<tr{% if r.headline and r.reach == "Both reaches" %} class="head-row"{% endif %}><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.table }}</td><td>{{ r.reach }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.f1 }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.p }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.r }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
<p class="note">Table A: the model trained on Sen1Floods11 (floods worldwide) and applied here unchanged. Table D: the model trained on the corridor's own reference windows, each window held out in turn, so no window is scored by a model that saw it.</p>
{% else %}
<p>There is no reference map for this date. The accuracy below was measured on the two events that do have one (Table D, pooled over both reaches); it describes the method, not this map.</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th class="r">F1, 2021</th><th class="r">F1, 2023</th><th class="r">Mean</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for r in b.score_rows %}<tr{% if r.headline %} class="head-row"{% endif %}><td>{{ r.name }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.f2021 }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.f2023 }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.mean }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2>How this map is made, and its limits</h2>
<details open><summary>What this bulletin is not</summary>
<ul class="limits">{% for a, t in b.not_this %}<li><b>{{ a }}</b> {{ t }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</details>
<details{% if b.print_mode %} open{% endif %}><summary>The models and the headline rule</summary>
<p>Three kinds of model map every event: a Random Forest, a U-Net and TerraMind-small (a pretrained Earth observation model, fine-tuned here). Each is the version trained on the hand-labelled Sen1Floods11 chips only; for TerraMind, of its two versions (radar only, or radar with terrain), the one that scored higher on Sen1Floods11's validation chips. Water within the permanent-water mask and cells in radar layover or shadow are removed from every map.</p>
<p>The headline map comes from the model with the highest pooled Table D F1 on GRD radar, averaged over 2021 and 2023; if the runner-up is not distinguishable from it (the paired interval includes zero), the faster model is used. For this bulletin: {{ b.head.rule }}.</p>
</details>
<details{% if b.print_mode %} open{% endif %}><summary>The trust layer</summary>
<p>Every cell has an incidence-angle class, a height-above-nearest-drainage (HAND) class and a valley-width class. For each class, Table D measured how often the headline model's flood calls were right (precision), averaged over 2021 and 2023. A cell's trust is the lowest of its three precisions: high at 0.40 or more, medium from 0.20, low below 0.20. A class with fewer than 100 reference flood pixels counts as low, because there is too little evidence. The rule was fixed on 8 October 2026, before the networks' Table D results existed. It rests on {{ b.trust_basis }}.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Terrain property</th><th>Class</th><th class="r">Precision (Table D)</th><th>Grade</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for r in b.trust_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.dim }}</td><td>{{ r.cls }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.p }}</td><td><span class="tag" style="background:{{ r.col }}">{{ r.grade }}</span></td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
{% if b.trust_scores %}<p><b>What each trust class means on the checked events.</b> The headline map of every validated event was scored against the hand-drawn reference inside each trust class (pooled over {{ b.trust_scores.windows_pooled }} windows; brackets: 95 % range from resampling the windows). Hit rate: share of the real flood the map found. False alarm ratio: share of the map's flood calls that were wrong. Critical success index (CSI): one score counting both (1 is perfect).</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Trust class</th><th class="r">Real flood in this class</th><th class="r">Hit rate</th><th class="r">False alarm ratio</th><th class="r">CSI</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{% for r in b.ts_rows %}<tr><td><span class="tag" style="background:{{ r.col }}">{{ r.name }}</span></td><td class="r">{{ r.share }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.hit }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.far }}</td><td class="r">{{ r.csi }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>
<p class="note">{{ b.trust_scores.caveat }} Radar-blind cells are never mapped as flood, so their hit rate is 0 by rule.</p>{% endif %}
</details>
<details{% if b.print_mode %} open{% endif %}><summary>Sources and files</summary>
<p class="note">{{ b.credits }}{% if b.worldpop %} People: WorldPop 2020 (CC BY 4.0).{% endif %}{% if b.forecast %} River forecasts: Copernicus Emergency Management Service, GloFAS (CC BY 4.0).{% endif %}</p>
<p class="note">Files for this event, in 06 Outputs\jalsar\{{ b.event.id }}\: {{ b.files|join(", ") }}.</p>
{% if b.event.strata_note %}<p class="note">Terrain strata: {{ b.event.strata_note }}</p>{% endif %}
</details>

<h2>Glossary</h2>
<details open><summary>Terms used in this bulletin</summary>
<dl class="gloss">
  <dt>Sentinel-1</dt><dd>The European radar satellites of the Copernicus programme. Radar sees through cloud and works at night, so it can map a flood during the monsoon when optical satellites see only cloud. The maps here use its 10 m grid.</dd>
  <dt>VV and VH</dt><dd>The two ways the radar sends and receives its pulse (vertical out, vertical or horizontal back). Water is dark in both.</dd>
  <dt>Relative orbit, ascending and descending pass</dt><dd>The track the satellite flew. An ascending pass flies north in the evening, a descending pass flies south in the morning; they see the valley sides from opposite directions.</dd>
  <dt>GRD and RTC</dt><dd>Two versions of the same radar image: GRD (ground range detected) as processed in Google Earth Engine, and RTC (radiometric terrain corrected) from ASF HyP3, which also evens out the brightness of slopes. The bulletin uses GRD.</dd>
  <dt>Radar blind (layover and shadow)</dt><dd>On steep slopes the radar either receives the top of the slope before its foot (layover) or cannot reach the far side at all (shadow). Nothing can be mapped there, so these cells are grey.</dd>
  <dt>HAND (height above nearest drainage)</dt><dd>How far a cell lies above the nearest stream, in metres, worked out from the elevation model. Flood water is usually low above the river.</dd>
  <dt>Permanent water</dt><dd>Water that is there in a normal year: cells with water at least half the time in the JRC Global Surface Water record, plus water on the February Sentinel-2 images. It is removed so that the normal river is not counted as flood.</dd>
  <dt>Sen1Floods11</dt><dd>A public set of Sentinel-1 image tiles from 11 floods around the world, with water drawn by hand. The models learned from it.</dd>
  <dt>Random Forest, U-Net, TerraMind</dt><dd>The three models. A Random Forest is 300 decision trees that each vote on one cell. A U-Net is a neural network that looks at each cell together with its neighbours. TerraMind-small is a large model pretrained by IBM and ESA on satellite images, fine-tuned here for water.</dd>
  <dt>Threshold</dt><dd>Each model gives a chance of water from 0 to 1. A cell counts as water when the chance is at or above the model's threshold, which was chosen on Sen1Floods11, never on this corridor.</dd>
  <dt>Headline model</dt><dd>The model whose map the bulletin shows first, chosen by its score on the corridor's checked events.</dd>
  <dt>Table A and Table D</dt><dd>Two ways of testing. Table A: train on Sen1Floods11 and apply to the corridor unchanged. Table D: train on the corridor's own hand-drawn windows, leaving out the window being scored each time.</dd>
  <dt>Precision, recall, F1</dt><dd>Precision: of the mapped flood, the share that is real. Recall (hit rate): of the real flood, the share that was mapped. F1: one score from the two, 1 is perfect.</dd>
  <dt>False alarm ratio and CSI</dt><dd>False alarm ratio: the share of the map's flood calls that were wrong. CSI (critical success index): correct flood cells divided by correct plus missed plus false flood cells; 1 is perfect.</dd>
  <dt>95 % interval</dt><dd>The range that the score would likely fall in with a different set of checked windows, found by redrawing the windows at random many times.</dd>
  <dt>Trust grade</dt><dd>High, medium or low, from how often the headline model's flood calls were right on the same kind of ground (incidence angle, HAND and valley width) on the checked events.</dd>
  <dt>Reach</dt><dd>A stretch of the river. Here: the gorge above Devprayag and the open valley below it.</dd>
  <dt>WorldPop 2020</dt><dd>A modelled map of where people live, on a grid of about 100 m, built from census totals, buildings and other data. It is an estimate, not a head count.</dd>
  <dt>Vulnerability class and relative risk</dt><dd>The vulnerability class (1 to 5) sums up twelve indicators of how hard a flood would hit a village. Relative risk adds whether the village has mapped flood and how many people are on it. Both compare villages within this corridor only.</dd>
  <dt>GloFAS, 2-year and 5-year flow</dt><dd>GloFAS is the Global Flood Awareness System, which forecasts river flow on a grid of about 5 km. The 2-year flow is a flow reached on average once in two years in GloFAS's own record; the 5-year flow once in five years.</dd>
  <dt>CWC</dt><dd>The Central Water Commission, which runs India's official flood forecasting and publishes warning and danger levels for river gauges.</dd>
  <dt>OpenStreetMap</dt><dd>A free map of the world made by volunteers. Roads, power lines and towers come from it, so anything nobody has mapped is missing.</dd>
</dl>
</details>

<footer class="rpt">{{ b.footer }}. Jal-SAR {{ b.version }}, bulletin made {{ b.made }}.</footer>
</div>

{% if not b.print_mode %}
<script type="application/json" id="gj-data">{{ b.village_json|replace("</", "<\\/")|safe }}</script>
<script>
var GJ={W:{{ b.map.w }},H:{{ b.map.h }},cell:{{ b.map.cell_m }},boxes:[{% for i in b.map.insets %}[{{ i.x }},{{ i.y }},{{ i.w }},{{ i.h }}]{{ "," if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}],
  spots:[{% for s in b.map.spots %}[{{ s.x }},{{ s.y }},{{ "%.4f"|format(s.km2) }},{{ "%.4f"|format(s.high_km2) }},"{{ s.trust }}"]{{ "," if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}],
  risk:{{ b.risk_colours|tojson }}, maroon:"{{ b.c.maroon }}"};
(function(){
  var svg=document.getElementById('gjmap'); if(!svg) return;
  var V=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('gj-data').textContent||'[]');
  var W=GJ.W,H=GJ.H,vb=[0,0,W,H],down=null,drag=null,vcol='plain',sel=null;
  var dots=[].slice.call(svg.querySelectorAll('circle.v')), spots=[].slice.call(svg.querySelectorAll('circle.spot'));
  var sized=[].slice.call(svg.querySelectorAll('[data-sw]')), texts=[].slice.call(svg.querySelectorAll('[data-fs]'));
  var on={};
  sized.forEach(function(e){e.setAttribute('vector-effect','non-scaling-stroke');});
  function box(){return svg.getBoundingClientRect();}
  function upp(){var r=box();return r.width>0?vb[2]/r.width:W/1000;}
  function fitAspect(c,w){var r=box(),a=(r.width||1000)/(r.height||400);var h=w/a;vb=[c[0]-w/2,c[1]-h/2,w,h];}
  function full(){var r=box(),a=(r.width||1000)/(r.height||400);
    if(a>W/H){var w=H*a;vb=[(W-w)/2,0,w,H];}else{var h=W/a;vb=[0,(H-h)/2,W,h];}}
  function nice(m){var c=[50,100,200,500,1000,2000,5000,10000,20000,50000];for(var i=c.length-1;i>=0;i--)if(c[i]<=m)return c[i];return c[0];}
  function set(){
    svg.setAttribute('viewBox',vb.join(' '));
    var u=upp(), z=Math.min(W/vb[2],H/vb[3]);
    var grow=z>8?1.3:(z>3?1.15:1);
    dots.forEach(function(c){c.setAttribute('r',(+c.dataset.px)*grow*u);});
    var showSpots=on.spots!==false&&z<=4;
    svg.querySelector('.lyr-spots').style.display=showSpots?'':'none';
    spots.forEach(function(c){c.setAttribute('r',(+c.dataset.px)*u);});
    sized.forEach(function(e){e.setAttribute('stroke-width',e.dataset.sw);
      if(e.dataset.dash){e.setAttribute('stroke-dasharray',e.dataset.dash.split(' ').map(function(x){return x*u;}).join(' '));}});
    texts.forEach(function(t){t.setAttribute('font-size',(+t.dataset.fs)*u);});
    [].forEach.call(svg.querySelectorAll('text.ilbl'),function(t){var b=GJ.boxes[+t.dataset.box];t.setAttribute('y',b[1]-6*u);});
    var g=document.getElementById('lbl-gorge'),l=document.getElementById('lbl-valley');
    if(g){var y=vb[1]+22*u;g.setAttribute('y',y);l.setAttribute('y',y);
      var sx=+svg.querySelector('.lyr-split line').getAttribute('x1');g.setAttribute('x',sx+8*u);l.setAttribute('x',sx-8*u);}
    if(sel!==null){var s=document.getElementById('gj-sel'),d=V[sel];s.setAttribute('cx',d.x);s.setAttribute('cy',d.y);s.setAttribute('r',(d.px*grow+5)*u);}
    var m=nice(120*u*GJ.cell);document.getElementById('gj-scale-t').textContent=m>=1000?(m/1000)+' km':m+' m';
    document.getElementById('gj-scale-b').style.width=(m/GJ.cell/u)+'px';
    document.getElementById('gj-zoom').textContent=z<1.05?'whole corridor':'zoom '+z.toFixed(1)+'x';
  }
  function pt(e){var r=box();return [vb[0]+(e.clientX-r.left)/r.width*vb[2],vb[1]+(e.clientY-r.top)/r.height*vb[3]];}
  window.gjZoom=function(f,c){c=c||[vb[0]+vb[2]/2,vb[1]+vb[3]/2];
    var w=Math.min(W*1.6,Math.max(W/400,vb[2]/f)),k=w/vb[2];
    vb=[c[0]-(c[0]-vb[0])*k,c[1]-(c[1]-vb[1])*k,w,vb[3]*k];set();};
  window.gjReset=function(){full();set();};
  window.gjTo=function(x,y,wm){fitAspect([x,y],wm);set();};
  window.gjBox=function(i){var b=GJ.boxes[i];gjTo(b[0]+b[2]/2,b[1]+b[3]/2,b[2]*1.6);
    document.getElementById('mapbox').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'});};
  window.gjFull=function(){var m=document.getElementById('mapbox');
    if(document.fullscreenElement){document.exitFullscreen();}else if(m.requestFullscreen){m.requestFullscreen();}};
  document.addEventListener('fullscreenchange',function(){var c=[vb[0]+vb[2]/2,vb[1]+vb[3]/2],w=vb[2];setTimeout(function(){fitAspect(c,w);set();},120);});
  window.addEventListener('resize',function(){var c=[vb[0]+vb[2]/2,vb[1]+vb[3]/2];fitAspect(c,vb[2]);set();});
  function f(x,n){return x===null||x===undefined?'n/a':Number(x).toLocaleString('en-IN',{maximumFractionDigits:n,minimumFractionDigits:n});}
  function esc(s){return String(s===null||s===undefined?'':s).replace(/[&<>"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;'}[c];});}
  function row(k,v){return '<tr><td>'+k+'</td><td class="r"><b>'+v+'</b></td></tr>';}
  window.gjShow=function(i,zoom){var d=V[i];if(!d)return;sel=i;
    var s=document.getElementById('gj-sel');s.style.display='';
    var h='<h4>'+esc(d.name)+'</h4><div class="where">'+esc(d.sub)+' sub-district, '+esc(d.district)+(d.block?'<br>'+esc(d.block):'')+'</div><table>';
    h+=row('Mapped flood in the village',f(d.flood,3)+' km&sup2;');
    h+=row('of it high trust',f(d.high,3)+' km&sup2;');
    h+=row('Share of the village area in the flood',d.share===null?'n/a':f(d.share*100,1)+' %');
    h+=row('Village area',f(d.vkm2,2)+' km&sup2;');
    if(d.wp_v!==null&&d.wp_v!==undefined){h+=row('People in the village (WorldPop 2020)',f(d.wp_v,0));
      h+=row('People on the flooded cells (WorldPop)',f(d.wp_f,0));}
    if(d.risk){h+=row('Risk (relative)','<span class="sw" style="background:'+(GJ.risk[d.risk]||'#9ca3af')+'"></span>'+esc(d.risk));
      h+=row('Vulnerability class (1 to 5)',d.vclass?esc(d.vclass)+' ('+esc(d.vuln)+')':'n/a');h+=row('Exposure class',esc(d.expo||'n/a'));}
    h+=row('Population, Census 2011',d.pop===null?'no census figure':f(d.pop,0));
    h+=row('Households, Census 2011',d.hh===null?'no census figure':f(d.hh,0));
    h+=row('Location',f(d.lat,4)+' N, '+f(d.lon,4)+' E');
    h+='</table><p class="note" style="margin:6px 0 0">Inside or touching the mapped flood does not mean damaged.</p>';
    h+='<div class="acts"><button type="button" onclick="gjTo('+d.x+','+d.y+','+(GJ.W/12)+')">Zoom here</button><button type="button" onclick="gjRow('+i+')">Show in the table</button></div>';
    document.getElementById('gj-card-body').innerHTML=h;document.getElementById('gj-card').classList.add('open');
    if(zoom){gjTo(d.x,d.y,GJ.W/12);}else{set();}};
  window.gjClose=function(){document.getElementById('gj-card').classList.remove('open');sel=null;document.getElementById('gj-sel').style.display='none';};
  function spotInfo(i){var s=GJ.spots[i];
    document.getElementById('gj-card-body').innerHTML='<h4>1 km square</h4><table>'+row('Mapped flood',f(s[2],3)+' km&sup2;')+row('of it high trust',f(s[3],3)+' km&sup2;')+row('Trust of most of it',esc(s[4]))+'</table><div class="acts"><button type="button" onclick="gjTo('+s[0]+','+s[1]+','+(GJ.W/40)+')">Zoom here</button></div>';
    document.getElementById('gj-card').classList.add('open');}
  svg.addEventListener('wheel',function(e){e.preventDefault();gjZoom(e.deltaY<0?1.25:0.8,pt(e));},{passive:false});
  svg.addEventListener('pointerdown',function(e){down={x:e.clientX,y:e.clientY,t:e.target};drag=pt(e);svg.classList.add('drag');svg.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);});
  svg.addEventListener('pointermove',function(e){if(!drag)return;var p=pt(e);vb[0]-=p[0]-drag[0];vb[1]-=p[1]-drag[1];set();});
  svg.addEventListener('pointerup',function(e){svg.classList.remove('drag');drag=null;
    if(down&&Math.abs(e.clientX-down.x)<5&&Math.abs(e.clientY-down.y)<5){var t=down.t;
      if(t.dataset&&t.dataset.vi!==undefined){gjShow(+t.dataset.vi);}
      else if(t.dataset&&t.dataset.box!==undefined){gjBox(+t.dataset.box);}
      else if(t.dataset&&t.dataset.si!==undefined){spotInfo(+t.dataset.si);}}
    down=null;});
  function paintDots(){dots.forEach(function(c){c.setAttribute('fill',vcol==='risk'?c.dataset.rcol:'#fff');});
    [].forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('.legend [data-for=vplain]'),function(e){e.style.display=vcol==='risk'||on.villages===false?'none':'';});
    [].forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('.legend [data-for=vrisk]'),function(e){e.style.display=vcol==='risk'&&on.villages!==false?'':'none';});}
  [].forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('#gj-layers input[data-lyr]'),function(cb){
    cb.addEventListener('change',function(){var k=cb.dataset.lyr;on[k]=cb.checked;
      [].forEach.call(svg.querySelectorAll('.lyr-'+k),function(e){e.style.display=cb.checked?'':'none';});
      if(k==='corr'){var o=svg.querySelector('.lyr-outside');if(o)o.style.display=cb.checked?'':'none';}
      [].forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('.legend [data-for="'+k+'"]'),function(e){e.style.display=cb.checked?'':'none';});
      if(k==='villages'){paintDots();if(!cb.checked)gjClose();}
      set();});});
  [].forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('#gj-layers input[name=vcol]'),function(r){r.addEventListener('change',function(){vcol=r.value;paintDots();});});
  var vt=document.getElementById('vt');
  if(vt){vt.tBodies[0].addEventListener('click',function(e){var tr=e.target.closest('tr');if(!tr)return;
    [].forEach.call(vt.querySelectorAll('tr.sel'),function(x){x.classList.remove('sel');});tr.classList.add('sel');
    gjShow(+tr.dataset.vi,true);document.getElementById('mapbox').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'});});}
  window.gjRow=function(i){var q=document.getElementById('vq');if(q)q.value='';
    var rows=[].slice.call(vt.tBodies[0].rows),k=0;rows.forEach(function(r,j){if(+r.dataset.vi===i)k=j;});
    gjState.vt=Math.floor(k/25);gjPage('vt',null);
    [].forEach.call(vt.querySelectorAll('tr.sel'),function(x){x.classList.remove('sel');});rows[k].classList.add('sel');
    rows[k].scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});};
  full();set();
})();
var gjState={};
function gjPage(id,step){
  var per=25,t=document.getElementById(id); if(!t) return;
  var q=(document.getElementById('vq')||{value:''}).value.toLowerCase();
  var rows=[].slice.call(t.tBodies[0].rows);
  var hit=rows.filter(function(r){return !q||r.textContent.toLowerCase().indexOf(q)>=0;});
  var pages=Math.max(1,Math.ceil(hit.length/per));
  var p=step===0?0:Math.min(pages-1,Math.max(0,(gjState[id]||0)+(step||0))); gjState[id]=p;
  rows.forEach(function(r){r.style.display='none';});
  hit.slice(p*per,p*per+per).forEach(function(r){r.style.display='';});
  document.getElementById(id+'-page').textContent='page '+(p+1)+' of '+pages;
  document.getElementById(id+'-count').textContent=hit.length+' of '+rows.length+' villages';
  var b=document.getElementById(id+'-pager').getElementsByTagName('button');
  b[0].disabled=p===0; b[1].disabled=p>=pages-1;
}
gjPage('vt',0);
</script>
{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
